                                </tr>
                                                                                                    <tr>
                                                                <td style="padding-left: 5px;padding-right: 5px;word-break: break-word">I do not have any personal criticism of you. However, as the Head of the Department, I would like to share one suggestion. Most lecturers teach almost entirely in Indonesian, even when international students are present. As a result, we sometimes miss important explanations and find it harder to understand the course compared to local students, while being assessed by the same standards.

I hope lecturers can use English more often, especially when explaining important concepts, assignments, and class discussions. I believe this would make the learning environment more inclusive and help international students succeed.</td>
                                </tr>
                                                                                                    <tr>
                                                                <td style="padding-left: 5px;padding-right: 5px;word-break: break-word">Disarankan untuk lebih sering mencairkan suasana ketika mengajar agar setiap mahasiswa mampu mengikuti mata kuliah dengan santai tapi serius</td>
                                </tr>
